# Console on hot paths (load / POS / dashboard)

Chrome DevTools serializes `console.log` / `console.info` on the **main thread**.
A loop that logs every paginated fetch or every longtask makes POS and dashboards
feel frozen. That already shipped once (`fb649cbaf` stripped 17 fetch logs).

## Forbidden on these files

`fetchAllRows.ts`, `POSSales.tsx`, `POSDashboard.tsx`, `Index.tsx`,
`cartMutators.ts`, `posCartPersistence.ts`, `usePosBilling.ts`,
`saleSettlement.ts`, `customerBalanceUtils.ts`, `customerBalanceCore.ts`,
`queryPersister.ts`.

- Do **not** add `console.log`, `console.info`, `console.debug`, or `console.time`.
- `console.error` / `console.warn` on real failures are OK.

## Diagnostics stay opt-in

New probes must use `diagConsoleInfo` from `src/lib/diagConsole.ts` (or an
existing flag: `ezzy_nav_perf`, `ezzy_cloud_usage`). Never log on every
render, fetch page, longtask, or tab switch.

In-memory rings + `window.__ezzy*.print()` are fine without a flag.

Do **not** auto-enable cloud-usage / fetch wrapping with `import.meta.env.DEV`.

## CI

`npm run check:console-guard` and `src/lib/hotPathConsole.guard.test.ts` fail
the build if the above returns. See `docs/console-perf-protections.md`.
